      "prompt": "Find a quadratic equation with real coefficients, written as $x^2+bx+c=0$, that has $3-2i$ as one of its roots.",
      "answer": "$x^2-6x+13=0$",
      "solution": {
        "steps": [
          "Because the coefficients are real, complex roots come in conjugate pairs, so $3+2i$ is also a root.",
          "Sum of the roots: $(3-2i)+(3+2i)=6$.",
          "Product of the roots: $(3-2i)(3+2i)=3^2-(2i)^2=9-4i^2=9-4(-1)=9+4=13$.",
          "For $x^2+bx+c=0$, we have $b=-(\\text{sum})=-6$ and $c=\\text{product}=13$.",
          "Therefore the quadratic is $x^2-6x+13=0$."
